  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "In an experiment to determine the velocity of sound in air at room temperature using a resonance tube, the first resonance is observed when the air column has a length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> for a tuning fork of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> is used. The velocity of the sound at room temperature is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>336</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The third resonance is observed when the air column has a length of _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "104",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Wavelength of wave <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>336</mn><mn>400</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>84</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>At first resonance</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>84</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi></math>&nbsp;is end correction.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />So third resonance length</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mn>21</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>104</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
